{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/30620-shakespeare-in-changeling","id":30620,"title":"Shakespeare in Changeling","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-15T15:38:40-08:00","id":30620,"title":"Shakespeare in Changeling","content":"Mad kings, backbiting courtiers, passion, destruction and a whole lot of scheming...what could be more Changeling than that? Can anyone think of ways of using the works of Shakespeare in Changeling that aren't immediately obvious as such? My group's gotten wise to my tendency to sneak literary references into games and I'd rather not have to give the habit up, if at all possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1664-thornfield13713","name":"Thornfield13713","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T15:41:18-08:00","id":30622,"title":"","content":"Well the most obvious is Midsummer Night's Dream, a lot of people seem to love doing that. But other ones are the reference to Queen Mab, she seems like one of the Gentry. And I love how Gargoyles handled Macbeth, as an immortal cursed by the Wyrd Sisters, so maybe its a Draconic Fairest whose Life/Wyrd is tied to an Ogre?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T09:29:36-08:00","id":31029,"title":"","content":"I recall reading a comic once (The Sandman) in which Shakespeare actually wrote a midsummer night's dream for the fae, and the characters were portraying actual fairies in the audience. Puck liked it so much that during the intermission he killed the actor playing him and took the his own role in the play, which I found delightful. It would certainly be an interesting way to introduce a new fairy to the plot.<br /> <br /> If you're looking for a more general Shakespeare based plot you could say a mad talecrafter is running around the city trying to make the freehold into the perfect story by tossing together elements of different Shakespere plays.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/807-arcadianawakened","name":"ArcadianAwakened","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T09:36:04-08:00","id":31033,"title":"","content":"Maybe try using some of his poetry instead of his plays? They're more obscure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T09:43:09-08:00","id":31727,"title":"","content":"The Dark Lady and the Fair Youth have a lot of speculation surrounding their identities, sometimes to the point of consituting folklore; they could easily be changelings (if so, I'd make the Dark Lady an elemental based on shadows rather than a darkling, and the Fair Youth the obvious choice of fairest).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T10:39:37-08:00","id":31771,"title":"","content":"Puck/Robin Goodfellow very much appears to be an actual Gentry that existed before the play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T11:22:49-08:00","id":31800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/30620-shakespeare-in-changeling?p=31727#post31727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dark Lady and the Fair Youth have a lot of speculation surrounding their identities, sometimes to the point of consituting folklore; they could easily be changelings (if so, I'd make the Dark Lady an elemental based on shadows rather than a darkling, and the Fair Youth the obvious choice of fairest).</div> </div> </div> </div>If hairs be wires, black wires grow on my lady's head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T12:42:24-08:00","id":31835,"title":"","content":"I wonder if Aeriel and Caliban from Tempest could be adapted somehow... Caliban could be an Ogre, while Aeriel may be a True Fae which is bound to a Mage because of a pledge?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T13:56:19-08:00","id":31883,"title":"","content":"Yeah Caliban could be a number of things.<br /> <br /> Oh maybe the Assassination of Caesar was more then what it seems? Maybe they used Iron Knives? Or after he died he turned into a pile of leaves and olive branches?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T12:20:18-08:00","id":40628,"title":"","content":"In the online comic weshadows Oberon is the son of Queen Mab and Julies Caesar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T00:23:37-08:00","id":40956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>moonwolf8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/30620-shakespeare-in-changeling?p=40628#post40628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the online comic weshadows Oberon is the son of Queen Mab and Julies Caesar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I think they took that idea from Gargoyles! The behind the scenes creators talk had a lot of ideas like that, and Queen Mab would have been in the show's further seasons if they didn't fire the Creator/showrunner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T09:31:37-08:00","id":57475,"title":"","content":"I have Shakespeare as a backround character in my game. One keeper has infiltrated Miami Freehold for her/his/its purposes. In past this Keeper was original Oberon and when visiting London he/she/it saw the Midsummernight Dream by King's Men. He/she/it became facinated by theatre and kidnapped Hamnet to Arcadia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2095-daider-santo","name":"Daider Santo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T16:54:03-08:00","id":60231,"title":"","content":"Shakespearean scholars can be a good source for learning Original Pronunciation, the accent his works were written in, which can be fun to give to all sorts of anachronistic fae creatures. It makes Shakespearean poetry rhyme and pace better, and it sounds delightfully Celtic, too. <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gPlpphT7n9s\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gPlpphT7n9s</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/486-foolish-milex","name":"Foolish Milex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T17:41:51-08:00","id":60258,"title":"","content":"I enjoy the idea that Romeo and Juliet may have been made into Darklings--the &quot;poisoned&quot; bodies left behind were just Kepper fakes. In fact I think it might be fun to flip the scrip on lots of characters from any source material, just to see them run against type and given some freshness.<br /> More traditionally, is Macbeth simply surrounded by Gravewights, or is it just the grave digger, Yorick, and the Dad's shade? And no matter what Ophilia has to have like a 3 Clarity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I also post a long form story, based on a Changeling: The Lost campaign at: <a href=\"https://www.fanfiction.net/s/10018173/1/Great-Fight-A-Twilight-Tommy-Tale\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.fanfiction.net/s/1001817...ght-Tommy-Tale</a><br /> I hope you will enjoy it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2020-gitariart","name":"GitariArt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T17:57:07-08:00","id":60266,"title":"","content":"A lot of good ideas have already been shared.... I set my Changeling game in Athens, Ohio to reference that <i><b>Midsummer Night's Dream</b></i> was in Athens. I look to Shakespeare for archetypes, then try to figure out ways to introduce them unexpectedly. Every game needs a wise fool and an eloquent villain, as well as some star-crossed lovers being thwarted by some blocking figure. Occasionally, these kinds of characters might be front and center, but more often I like to have them going on in the background to give the court or community a sense of depth.<br /> <br /> I'm also a sucker for <b><i>The Tempest</i></b>:Prospero is a Keeper and Miranda (fairest), Caliban (beast), and Ariel (Elemental) all suffer under his rule. But maybe that's too obvious? How about modifying As You Like It? The brother of your local court's king is kicked out of the freehold and into the Hedge for suspected treason, exiled with him is some character that one of the players has grown attached to. When the motley goes into the woods, there are Ogre drug dealers (Silvius and Phebe) that drag one of them into a triangle despite the PC's disinterest. A lesser-known work that was only partly written by Shakespeare is <i><b>Pericles, Prince of Tyre</b></i>. I like the start of the play as an idea: the hand of a beauty can be won by solving a riddle, but the riddle is a horrible trap that will cause the suitor to be executed whether he is right or wrong....<br /> <br /> Pericles: <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pericles,_Prince_of_Tyre\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pericles,_Prince_of_Tyre</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2002-quynce","name":"Quynce","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2002_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-28T19:45:52-08:00","id":60341,"title":"","content":"A man has fallen in love with a changeling, an aloof woman with immaculate taste and a smile that warms like the sun. He has has known her long enough to know that it would take something really special in order to win her attention. Asking around, he learns of a night market held in the sketchier part of the city and attends it one strange night of the new moon. There, he meets a strange goblin usurer who promises to lend him the means &quot;to be a proper suitor,&quot; in exchange for a some service or collateral that will inevitably fall through. If the bond falls through, the goblin merchant has a sharp knife and a promise of a pound of flesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}